Nations System Code of Conduct UNTERM Visualizations and machine readability Home News and media Announcements Announcements Global Language Register Examination for Spanish Interpreters 07/28/2026 The United Nations Department for General Assembly and Conference Management (DGACM) is accepting applications until 5 August 2026 for the Global Language Register examination for Spanish Interpreters. Successful candidates will be placed on the DGACM Global Language Register and may be offered temporary appointments under the “When Actually Employed” (WAE) modality. The examination is open to qualified candidates whose main language is Spanish and who have an excellent knowledge of English and French. Additional eligibility requirements are detailed on the United Nations Careers website. The positions are located in DGACM at the United Nations Office at Vienna. Competitive Examination for German Translators 01/19/2026 The United Nations is accepting applications for the competitive examination for German translators until 24 February 2026. The examination is open to qualified candidates with a&nbsp;perfect&nbsp;command of&nbsp;English and&nbsp;German&nbsp;(UN Level IV). For this job opening,&nbsp;either Spanish or French&nbsp;is&nbsp;also&nbsp;required.&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;requirements are detailed on the UN Careers website (in English and French ). Competitive Examination for Spanish Translators, Editors and Verbatim Reporters 04/17/2025 The United Nations is accepting applications for the competitive examination for Spanish translators, editors and verbatim reporters until 10 May 2025. The examination is open to qualified candidates with a perfect command of Spanish, which should be their main language, as well as an excellent knowledge of English. Excellent knowledge of at least one other official language of the United Nations is desirable and will be an advantage. Applications from candidates with excellent knowledge of Arabic or Russian are strongly encouraged. Additional requirements are detailed on the UN Careers website ( English and French ).&nbsp;&nbsp; Eighth MoU Conference 03/21/2025 The Eighth MoU Conference will take place on 7 and 8 April 2025 at the Vienna International Centre, in a hybrid format, under the theme “Language professions embrace change”.&nbsp;Co-hosted by the Department for General Assembly and Conference Management (DGACM) and Saint-Joseph University of Beirut, the Conference will bring together representatives of DGACM and universities with which it has established memorandums of understanding (MoUs). It will be an opportunity to share experiences and best practices in preparing language professionals for careers at the United Nations, and more broadly, to discuss the latest trends and developments in the field. Competitive Examination for Arabic Interpreters 07/10/2024 The United Nations is accepting applications for the competitive examination for Arabic interpreters until 4 August 2024. The examination will be conducted online. It is open to qualified candidates with a perfect command of Arabic, which is normally expected to be their main language. Candidates must also be fluent in English or French as an active interpretation language. The eligibility criteria and the application process are detailed in the announcement, available in English and French . Competitive Examination for French Translators, Editors and Verbatim Reporters 05/21/2024 The United Nations is accepting applications for the competitive examination for",
